<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Q1 coconut oil exports seen down.</title>
<headline>Philippine Q1 coconut oil exports seen down.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine coconut products exports in the first three months could reach 340,886 tonnes, according to preliminary data from trade group United Coconut Association of the Philippines Inc.</p>
<p>UCAP said the country exported a total of 552,239 tonnes of coconut products in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Preliminary data showed the country's coconut oil exports from January to March dropped by 31.8 percent to 214,758 tonnes compared with 314,897 tonnes in the same period last year.  </p>
<p>UCAP said Philippine exports of coconut products include copra, coconut oil, dessicated coconut and oleochemicals.</p>
<p>The trade group did not give a reason for the drop in exports.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
